The project will be conducted progressively, with a pilot phase on one office or one mission line followed by progressive generalization. Change management support and training are expected to ensure a smooth transition. Ideally, the pilot should be operational before the next closing/tax campaign.

Our proposal meets all the requirements outlined in the call for tenders, including quality and relevance of the solution, reliability and traceability of outputs, confidentiality and security, respect of professional secrecy and auditor independence, data sovereignty, quality of integration with Cabinet Vauclair & Associés' production tools, total cost, quality of support, environmental considerations, and capacity for innovation. We believe that our Atelier platform offers a robust non-decisional assistance tool that improves productivity, quality, and reliability of work while preserving professional secrecy and the reliability of figures.
